<title>INDIA: Indian soybean, soyoil end firm on thin volumes.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean, soyoil end firm on thin volumes.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices ended firm in the central Indian markets on Thursday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Prices were up by 200-250 rupees per tonne on good demand from processing plants, they said.</p>
<p>The sowing operations was in full swing.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were firm on good local demand. Soyoil solvent was up by 100 rupees and soyoil refined was up by 200 rupees per tonne today. But the business volume was dull, traders said.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were firm following good export enquiries, traders said.</p>
<p>Soymeal yellow was $267-269 per tonne FAS (free alongside ship) west coast Indian ports for exports. Rapeseed extraction was $102-104 per tonne FAS in bulk for export and was 3,350-3,450 rupees per tonne in FOR (free on rail) condition.</p>
